# Rust
target/
**/*.rs.bk
# Container-run cargo target dirs. `target/` alone did not cover these: an
# ad-hoc `docker run -v "$PWD:/w"` build with a different CARGO_TARGET_DIR
# writes here, and a `git add -A` then swept 27,945 files and ~9 GB of
# incremental build output into the repository. Glob, not two literals, so the
# next variant is caught before it is committed rather than after.
target-*/
**/target-*/

# OS image build outputs
os/images/out/

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
._*

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Demo VM working files (tools/punar-up.sh caches the image outside the repo)
punar-vars.fd
